---
import Layout from '../layouts/WorkspaceLayout.astro'
import { GUIDES, TOPICS } from '../lib/guides'
const software = { '@type': 'SoftwareApplication', '@id': 'https://veqtor.pro/#software', name: 'Veqtor Workspace', applicationCategory: 'ProductivityApplication', operatingSystem: 'macOS', url: 'https://veqtor.pro/', installUrl: 'https://veqtor.pro/setup', description: 'Read, edit and save Word files with your AI assistant. Changes go into your document, ready to review.' }
---
<Layout canonicalPath="/" structuredData={software} title="Veqtor Workspace — Ask AI. Get the changes in Word." description="Read, edit and save Word files with your AI assistant. Veqtor Workspace puts the changes into your document, ready to review. For macOS.">
  <section class="shell concept-hero" aria-labelledby="home-title">
    <div>
      <p class="concept-kicker">Your documents. Your AI assistant.</p>
      <h1 id="home-title">Ask AI. Get the changes in Word.</h1>
      <p class="hero-description">Veqtor Workspace lets your AI assistant read, edit and save Word files on your Mac. Describe what you need. The changes go into your document, ready to review.</p>
      <p class="hero-benefit">No copying text back and forth.</p>
      <div class="concept-actions"><a class="concept-button primary" href="/setup">Get started <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="concept-button" href="#examples">See examples <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div>
      <div class="concept-availability"><span class="availability-dot">For macOS</span><span>Claude Desktop &amp; ChatGPT Desktop</span></div>
    </div>
    <figure class="hero-example">
      <div class="example-request"><span class="example-label">You ask in the chat</span><p>“Change the delivery period to 45 days. Use tracked changes and add a comment explaining the edit.”</p></div>
      <div class="document-window">
        <div class="document-toolbar"><span class="document-file"><span class="word-symbol" aria-hidden="true">W</span>Delivery plan</span><span>Tracked changes</span></div>
        <div class="document-paper"><p class="document-eyebrow">Project overview</p><h3>Delivery timeline</h3><p>The final deliverables will be ready within <del>30</del> <ins>45</ins> days of the project start date.</p><div class="document-comment"><strong>Your name · Comment</strong>Updated the delivery period to 45 days, as requested.</div></div>
      </div>
      <figcaption>Review the change in Word.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="concept-section" id="examples" aria-labelledby="examples-title">
    <div class="shell" data-tabs>
      <p class="concept-kicker">A few things to try</p>
      <h2 id="examples-title">Tell AI what you want done.</h2>
      <div class="example-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Document examples">
        <button type="button" role="tab" id="tab-draft" aria-controls="panel-draft" aria-selected="true">Revise a draft</button>
        <button type="button" role="tab" id="tab-comments" aria-controls="panel-comments" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">Add comments</button>
        <button type="button" role="tab" id="tab-file" aria-controls="panel-file" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">Edit your working file</button>
      </div>
      <div class="example-panel" id="panel-draft" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-draft">
        <div><h3>Make the wording specific.</h3><div class="example-request"><span class="example-label">Your request</span><p>“Clarify what ‘transferable’, ‘available’ and ‘traceable’ mean in this clause. Make the requirements explicit. Use tracked changes.”</p></div><p class="example-note">The revised wording is in the Word file. Read each addition, then accept or reject it.</p></div>
        <figure class="example-output example-figure">
          <div class="document-window"><div class="document-toolbar"><span class="document-file"><span class="word-symbol" aria-hidden="true">W</span>Agreement</span><span>Tracked changes</span></div><a class="document-screenshot" href="/examples/word-clarity.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="Open the Word excerpt at full size"><img src="/examples/word-clarity.png" width="570" height="259" loading="lazy" alt="A Word clause with tracked additions defining transferable processes as including documentation and technical support; available materials as freely sourced from suppliers; and traceable materials as having documented supply chains." /></a></div>
          <figcaption><span>Word document excerpt</span><a href="/examples/word-clarity.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View full size ↗</a></figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
      <div class="example-panel" id="panel-comments" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-comments" hidden>
        <div><h3>Put your notes in the document.</h3><div class="example-request"><span class="example-label">Your request</span><p>“Add comments to the relevant clauses: payment is due 45 days in advance; rights are granted upon the first payment. Keep the document text unchanged.”</p></div><p class="example-note">Record decisions where they belong. The comments stay with the Word file.</p></div>
        <figure class="example-output example-figure">
          <div class="document-window"><div class="document-toolbar"><span class="document-file"><span class="word-symbol" aria-hidden="true">W</span>Agreement</span><span>Comments</span></div>
            <div class="word-comments">
              <div class="word-comment"><div class="word-comment-meta"><strong>Shilov, Ilya</strong><span>2 minutes ago</span></div><p>Negotiation outcome: payment is due 45 days in advance.</p><div class="word-comment-actions"><span><svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 5H3v10h4l3 3v-3h7V5h-3M10 2 7 5l3 3M7 5h7" /></svg>Reply</span><span><svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6H2v9h4l3 3v-3h8V9M9 4l3 3 6-6" /></svg>Resolve</span></div></div>
              <div class="word-comment"><div class="word-comment-meta"><strong>Shilov, Ilya</strong><span>A few seconds ago</span></div><p>Negotiation outcome: rights are granted upon the first payment.</p><div class="word-comment-actions"><span><svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 5H3v10h4l3 3v-3h7V5h-3M10 2 7 5l3 3M7 5h7" /></svg>Reply</span><span><svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6H2v9h4l3 3v-3h8V9M9 4l3 3 6-6" /></svg>Resolve</span></div></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </figure>
      </div>
      <div class="example-panel" id="panel-file" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-file" hidden>
        <div><h3>Make the changes. Save the file.</h3><div class="example-request"><span class="example-label">Your request</span><p>“Change the review period from 20 to 40 business days and allow objections by email. Use tracked changes. Save the changes to this file.”</p></div><p class="example-note">Update your working file or ask for a new version. You choose where the result is saved.</p></div>
        <figure class="example-output example-figure"><div class="document-window"><div class="document-toolbar"><span class="document-file"><span class="word-symbol" aria-hidden="true">W</span>Working agreement</span><span>Tracked changes</span></div><div class="document-paper working-file-paper"><p>The Client has <del>20</del> <ins>40</ins> business days to review the Deliverables. Any objections must be sent in writing <ins>(including by email)</ins> within those <del>20</del> <ins>40</ins> business days.</p></div></div></figure>
      </div>
      <p class="sample-caption">Just need to read? Ask for a summary or an explanation and leave the file unchanged.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="concept-section" aria-labelledby="how-title">
    <div class="shell"><p class="concept-kicker">How it works</p><h2 id="how-title">From a request to a saved document.</h2>
      <div class="flow-grid">
        <div class="flow-step"><span class="flow-number">01</span><h3>Point to your documents</h3><p>Save your Word file. Point the assistant to it and any documents it should use for context: contracts, reports, certificates or other records.</p></div>
        <div class="flow-step"><span class="flow-number">02</span><h3>Describe the task</h3><p>Ask the assistant to read, edit or comment. Request tracked changes when you want each edit to stay visible.</p></div>
        <div class="flow-step"><span class="flow-number">03</span><h3>Save and review</h3><p>Ask it to update the file or save a new version. Open the result in Word to review it.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="concept-section installation-callout" aria-labelledby="install-title">
    <div class="shell installation-inner"><div><p class="concept-kicker">Start here</p><h2 id="install-title">Add Veqtor to your assistant.</h2><p>Choose Claude Desktop or ChatGPT Desktop, then try a small edit.</p></div><a class="concept-button primary" href="/setup">Installation guide <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
  </section>

  <section class="concept-section" id="questions" aria-labelledby="questions-title">
    <div class="shell faq-grid"><div><p class="concept-kicker">Good to know</p><h2 id="questions-title">A few practical questions.</h2></div>
      <div class="questions">
        <details><summary>What do I need?</summary><p>A Mac and Claude Desktop or ChatGPT Desktop with local tools enabled. Codex also works. Veqtor connects to your assistant; it does not include an AI model. Your AI service’s account and usage terms still apply. See the installation guide for the current connection steps.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What happens to my original file?</summary><p>Veqtor keeps a snapshot and gives the assistant a working copy. You can ask it to save a new file or update the original. Before replacing the original, it checks for saved changes made since the task began. Save your Word edits first, avoid editing the same file during a save, and reopen it afterwards.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Does my document stay on my Mac?</summary><p>The files and Veqtor’s working copies are on your Mac. Content returned to your assistant becomes part of your AI conversation and may be processed by its provider. Local files do not mean a fully offline AI workflow.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Which documents can I use?</summary><p>The current focus is Word files and text-based PDFs used as supporting material. Scanned PDFs need separate text recognition. Always check the result, including formatting and comments, before using or sharing it.</p></details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="concept-section"><div class="shell guide-band"><div><h3>Working on a contract?</h3><p>{GUIDES.length} guides across {TOPICS.length} topics, in the existing contract library.</p></div><a href="/guides">Explore the guides <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>
</Layout>
